<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian govt sees jobs from profits growth.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian govt sees jobs from profits growth.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Government Senate Leader Robert Hill said on Monday strong business profits would produce jobs.</p>
<p>&quot;Those business profits will be reinvested in the Australian economy, providing jobs,&quot; Hill told the upper house.</p>
<p>&quot;In the December quarter we had a record of A$12 billion of profits. That's good for the Australian economy,&quot; Hill said.  </p>
<p>Official data last week showed pre-tax profits of Australian companies with more than 30 employees rose 8.6 percent in the December quarter to A$12.024 billion from A$11.071 billion in the September quarter.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
